{"status":"completed","summary":"Repaired and secured the node1 status service. It now runs automatically as statusd over run/status.sock, permits statusd and status-readers members, denies outsider, validates the STATUS protocol, and survives reboot with the status document unchanged.","actions_performed":["Created statusd, status-reader, outsider, and status-readers with the required role membership.","Repaired server.py to serve only STATUS followed by a newline and return ERROR for other requests.","Installed and enabled a hardened statusd.service using the existing Python runtime.","Applied statusd:status-readers ownership and restrictive directory/socket permissions.","Verified authorized access, unauthorized denial, invalid-request handling, cleanup, and reboot persistence."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Discovery and protected-data baseline","command_ids":["cmd-28f9aa6aa94f4999","cmd-048715c5886346d5"],"summary":"Captured RHEL 10.0, kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0, Python 3.12.9, SELinux Enforcing, missing service/accounts/socket, original source, and document SHA-256."},{"requirement":"Repair and automatic service operation","command_ids":["cmd-ae0d747cf2b640ce","cmd-e99d04a636374101"],"summary":"The validated systemd unit is enabled and active; after reboot it automatically returned as statusd with group status-readers."},{"requirement":"Owner/group-only socket boundary","command_ids":["cmd-9e52231dd49047e1","cmd-168c1471e40247cc"],"summary":"statusd and status-reader successfully read through the socket, while outsider receives PermissionError. The socket is statusd:status-readers mode 0660 within a mode-0750 runtime directory."},{"requirement":"Protocol validation","command_ids":["cmd-9e52231dd49047e1","cmd-168c1471e40247cc"],"summary":"Exact STATUS newline requests return the document; multiple invalid requests return exactly ERROR newline."},{"requirement":"Status document preservation","command_ids":["cmd-28f9aa6aa94f4999","cmd-e210198643b142c3","cmd-e99d0